separately under MIT; the MIT licence does NOT cover catalog/.

Every value in the catalog cites its source by id; the full list of sources, their licences and the date their
terms were reviewed is in sources.yaml. Values are stated as single facts with citations; no source's prose,
tables, lists or images are reproduced.

Attributions and additional terms
---------------------------------

FAO (ECOCROP, DAD-IS)
  Values derived from FAO databases are used under CC BY 4.0 and the FAO database terms of use
  (https://www.fao.org/contact-us/terms/db-terms-of-use/en/). Citation format:
    FAO. [year]. ECOCROP. Accessed on [date]. https://ecocrop.apps.fao.org/ Licence: CC-BY-4.0.
    FAO. [year]. Domestic Animal Diversity Information System (DAD-IS). Accessed on [date].
      https://www.fao.org/dad-is/en/ Licence: CC-BY-4.0.
  Additional FAO terms that apply to these values: they may not be used to promote a commercial enterprise,
  and their use does not imply any endorsement by FAO.
  ECOCROP values were read from the table shipped in the Recocrop R package (CRAN, GPL-3 code); only FAO's data
  is used, not the package's code.

EPPO Codes
  Contains EPPO Codes (www.eppo.int). Download date: recorded with each import in sources.yaml / the
  value's source locator.

Wikipedia
  Companion-planting pairs from "List of companion plants" (Wikipedia contributors), CC BY-SA 4.0, pinned
  revision recorded in each value's source locator.

FAO-56
  Crop coefficients, stage lengths, root depths and depletion fractions are cited as facts from
  Allen, R.G., Pereira, L.S., Raes, D. and Smith, M. (1998). Crop evapotranspiration. FAO Irrigation and
  Drainage Paper 56. FAO, Rome.

Private packs
-------------
A CropStack server may also load a private pack from its own data volume (<data>/catalog-private/). Private
packs are personal, are never part of this repository or its releases, and are not covered by this NOTICE.
